#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:5
#: 68b6e99ff7d146ec8bea34486d842aeb
msgid "FrSky Telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:7
#: f25e2fc2b58b49c1aba3585b3644b635
msgid "FrSky telemetry allows you to display ArduPilot information such as flight modes, battery level, and error messages, as well as information from additional FrSky sensors on `OpenTx <https://www.open-tx.org/>`__ compatible RC transmitters and even older X9R transmitters (although with more limited capability)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:9
#: cf2d90a2adad47bdb85fa859a6c6b28f
msgid "It is particularly useful:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:10
#: 0b745bd2358b4da6a132c99c2a129c57
msgid "for flying without a ground control station (no need for MAVLink telemetry radio),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:11
#: 5367f1cfefc84e01aac235a4601e1bb1
msgid "as a backup in case the ground station fails (e.g., loss of MAVLink radio link),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:12
#: 538920ea1c2c427ca4e75850c7c0afdd
msgid "when a separate person operates the ground control station,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:13
#: 6676052cb5074307b6a32ce8980af473
msgid "for quick situational awareness by the pilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:15
#: cbc40faaff824ff48f688b166a4a038a
msgid "Moreover, some RC transmitters such as the Taranis series, Horus, and T16, can be configured to play sounds, vibrate or perform automatic RC actions based on telemetry information through the highly configurable OpenTX firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:21
#: 077f15c38ed9420ea226131a53ac35b7
msgid "Common FrSky Telemetry Setup with OpenTX transmitter running :ref:`FlightDeck <common-frsky-flightdeck>` or :ref:`Yaapu Telemetry Script <common-frsky-yaapu>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:23
#: 60dab9dfb7344a608e14cceec8cab785
msgid "before the addition of FrSky telemetry protocols to ArduPilot, it was necessary to use an external converter to convert normal MAVLink telemetry from the Autopilot into FrSky Sport compatible telemetry (See :ref:`common-frsky-mavlink`), but this is no longer required. However, the `MAV2PT converter <https://www.rcgroups.com/forums/showthread.php?3089648-Mavlink-To-FrSky-Passthrough-Converter>`__ is especially useful for converting MAVLink telemetry output from many long-range RC systems for display on an OpenTX transmitter or forwarding via Bluetooth or WiFi to a smarphone or PC running a Ground Control Station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:27
#: 2968a39474674806aee58cb45aaadf18
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:29
#: bf6e7c07d4d4461fab38ec84a6e0cb58
msgid "In order to use FrSky telemetry, the following steps are required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:31
#: 258427110e9642019f70aeef45f2b024
msgid "Connect an autopilot telemetry port to an FrSky receiver which has an SPort or Fport interface. This may require a bi-directional inverter depending on which autopilot it being used. See :ref:`common-connecting-sport-fport`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:32
#: f3460b76c7ba4f28878a6ba9b89128bb
msgid "Configure the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:33
#: d50bae0e011142edac1ba7887315354c
msgid "Install a LUA script to display the full telemetry. (Although is it possible to display a subset of telemetry values using OpenTX's built in telemetry screens, it is very limited.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:37
#: b56ec0a81d52492085c69c3ca52092b0
msgid "Connection Diagrams"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:39
#: 820ae6fe61534d4ea4c58e06e873fc9c
msgid "See"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:45
#: 4875ad7bccc647639fbe6026768ad4c8
msgid "for connection diagrams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:49
#: b7cf75e6bf314e11bc8afaac00eb3c64
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:51
#: 7ae751b60edf4b5f8f1dcdee18e341a7
msgid "Two protocols are available, Repurposed and PassThrough. Repurposed has been superseded by PassThrough since much more telemetry information can be transferred and displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:53
#: caa8f30164474c94bb4f2e37faaf3a9b
msgid "First set the SERIALxPROTOCOL to \"10\" for the telemetry port used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:55
#: 03462cb822c743128fa3c7dc5a1b3d5a
msgid "SERIAL port numbers do not necessarily directly correspond to UART or TELEM port labels. See the hardware documentation for your :ref:`autopilot <common-autopilots>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:57
#: 89cc892eb3d14e969d08eadcf41d7367
msgid "If you have an F7 or H7 autopilot, and therefore do not need to use an external inverter, you must turn on the inverters for the SERIAL port and also set it to half duplex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:59
#: 793b2e8b41d342abb670087c11c0885f
msgid "Any configuration change to a UART requires a re-boot to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:62
#: a71b4d4c088e471688dd3a0499e02e8a
msgid "In general, F4 based autopilots using an external bi-directional inverter can use any UART with the following configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:64
#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:69
#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:77
#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:82
#: 7a3ba757d208418890e031a59e0e0f12
#: b5a67ba9bc2844afbb688dd34e3bf924
#: 71f71faa32424ffa9de8de85c0b1e472
#: 2cb1a2dba1e14a87b0a53628f0445670
msgid "``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` =10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:65
#: f5745d2416f34396a2be05043f17617b
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` =160 (enable pull-up/pull-downs on TX and RX pins for those external inverter circuits that may require it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:67
#: 06a1dd3f296b40f19febccf1190a38d4
msgid "F4 based autopilots using an \"inverted SPort\" output from the receiver can connect it to any  UART's TX pin with the configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:70
#: 46352a20a0d34e8095bd0709a165c3e9
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 4 (Half Duplex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:72
#: a2de60a5826f40dea39cfb79fe8b1ce6
msgid "F4 based autopilots cannot use the RX pin with an \"inverted SPort\" output since the SWAP capability is only available in F7/H7 based autopilots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:75
#: 073626a6beee4f28b69bcc021720a54f
msgid "F7/H7 based autopilots can directly connect to the TX pin of any UART and use this configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:78
#: f7acb7540fa34a1e85efec44a115d322
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` =  7 (invert TX/RX,Half Duplex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:80
#: 64aa1d8f206e4fd8b6369f6f1b227fd1
msgid "OR to the RX pin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:83
#: 187d5190e9134d3cb3dc11c22ddb7984
msgid "``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` =  15 (invert TX/RX,Half Duplex, SWAP TX/RX pins)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:86
#: 6abb80867be94949b3e6485b5f11e7d1
msgid "Some F7/H7 autopilots have level/shifters on their UARTs that cause a delay in Half Duplex operation, like CubeOrange. If the above configuration does not, try setting :ref:`RC_OPTIONS<RC_OPTIONS>` = 8 which will add padding in the protocol to accommodate this. However, using this option when not required will break operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:88
#: 02c59e14cc284fd59ba639df1835f047
msgid "Set :ref:`FRSKY_OPTIONS<FRSKY_OPTIONS>` bit 0 to \"1\" to enable sending alternating airspeed and groundspeed data to the display script. The :ref:`Yaapu FrSky Telemetry Script for OpenTX <common-frsky-yaapu>` can use this but it may cause other display apps/scripts to alternate the speed value readout."
msgstr ""

