#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:102
#: a515339a88154fc98a76f240981498f8
msgid "Turnigy 9XR Pro"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:104
#: e2ddbe205b0242d9bc364e6195ba8556
msgid "This section describes how to enable FrSky telemetry on the Turnigy 9XR Pro transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:108
#: c921f8eabe094aceaa25aa6e746b18e6
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:110
#: c19d759fd285418f84e44d6ce4d8b839
msgid "You will need a transmitter module with support for FrSky telemetry, such as the ``FrSky XJT``.  The DJT_ also supports telemetry, but you will need to use an external cable to connect the telemetry data from the module to your transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:115
#: 003a074766ae4ecb8488b106ae59d878
msgid "The instructions in this section are specifically for the XJT module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:118
#: 9b1930c4e36642a79cfa2a7e58fb7397
msgid "You will need to be running a recent version (211 or later) of the ErSky9x firmware.  You can find more information about upgrading the firmware and about ErSky9x in general from `the documentation`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:128
#: a07851109f484aa1b2c216460afdf883
msgid "Configuring ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:130
#: 72450fe6a165480aa1a09d2e85f84a1f
msgid "Ensure that you have the appropriate ``SERIAL#_PROTOCOL`` parameter set to ``10`` (\"passthrough FrSky telemetry\") to select the ArduPilot SPORT protocol.  For example, if you have plugged your SmartPort cable into the serial 4/5 port on your Pixhawk, set ``SERIAL4_PROTOCOL`` to ``10``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:136
#: 6783d331a3bf4142a05e157cbd0032c6
msgid "Reboot your controller after making this change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:138
#: 6d01ae305b7149ca998c8051c18eabac
msgid "ErSky9x will also work with protocol ``4`` (\"repurposed FrSky telemetry\"), but you will not have access to ArduPilot-specific information such as the name of the current flight mode or arming status."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:144
#: a3d5dcb40f8343a9b7ab06671dcba9b6
msgid "Configuring the 9XR Pro"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:146
#: 6958934d82254c178ac87d1d8fdd34d9
msgid "Verify that you are running version 211 or later.  Navigate to the ``Radio Setup`` menu and then select ``Version``.  Look at the ``SVN`` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:154
#: 5bd6b422a21a4caf926c8db21436a7bd
msgid "Telemetry support is substantially improved in revision 218 and later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:157
#: 17249eb0efee4e0db2dd192f99144e65
msgid "Navigate to ``Model Setup`` menu, then select ``Protocol``.  Ensure that you have ``Proto`` set to ``XJT``, and ``Type`` set to ``D16``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:164
#: e8d3fe7baceb423f989b81a856be8c01
msgid "In older versions of the firmware, you may see `PXX` instead of `XJT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:167
#: d6e68c6e6b1248a1aa5b94c2e248d7b4
msgid "Navigate to the ``Model Setup`` menu, then select ``Telemetry``, and then again select ``Telemetry`` from the popup menu.  Ensure that ``UsrProto`` is set to ``ArduP`` (for ArduPlane) or ``ArduC`` (for ArduCopter), ``Telemetry Com Port`` (previously ``FrSky Com Port``) is ``1``, and ``Com Port Invert`` (previously ``Invert Com 1``) is off (unchecked)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:182
#: 4ccc9a5e419e4ea4bf88a6cf906bedad
msgid "If you are using something other than ArduPlane or ArduCopter, you can set ``UsrProto`` to ``FrSky``.  You will get a more basic telemetry display that will be missing things like the graphic heading indicator, the name of the current flight mode, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:188
#: 96cae15f8b2d44d3b21526ec2ec7d992
msgid "At this point, you should be receiving extended telemetry on your 9XR Pro.  If you navigate to the telemetry home screen (use the up/down arrows to switch between screens) you should see standard FrSky telemetry values (such as RSSI, receiver voltage, etc) as well as extended telemetry, such as flight mode, current measurements, GPS information, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:199
#: 4084bc4a7e12407aadcc15793cf9a9cd
msgid "Use the left/right arrows to switch between available telemetry views:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:206
#: 4fe1f372e1b8450d9e4285cd7a1f7217
msgid "Configuring custom telemetry screens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-frsky-telemetry.rst:208
#: 85c9d2ebf5c3423f84bfa6446fed138d
msgid "ErSky9x allows you to customize two telemetry display screens with your choice of information.  To configure the custom screens, navigate to ``Model Setup``, then select ``Telemetry``, and then select ``Custom``:"
msgstr ""

